{"parentUuid":"69932146-c327-4bf9-adf2-77203761e45d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5e26f85c-e78c-4ba3-bfbb-b4195fba49df","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UGVH192rCFtmHa6553K1SB","type":"tool_result","content":"================================================================================\n[Copilot] cmd/entire/cli/plugin_store.go:81\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPluginDataDir joins the plugin name directly into a filesystem path. Since isPluginCandidate currently allows \".\" and \"..\" (it only rejects slashes), a plugin named \".\" or \"..\" would cause filepath.Join to collapse the path (e.g., <root>/data/.. → <root>), breaking the per-plugin isolation and enabling writes outside the intended data subdir. Consider rejecting \".\"/\"..\" (and/or validating that the final path stays within <root>/data) inside PluginDataDir (and ideally in isPluginCandidate too) so ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR is always a dedicated per-plugin directory.\n\n\n================================================================================\n[Copilot] cmd/entire/cli/plugin_store.go:291\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nstripPluginExeExt currently strips .exe/.bat/.cmd regardless of OS. On non-Windows, the dispatcher resolves only `entire-<name>` (no PATHEXT behavior), so accepting/installing `entire-foo.bat` (or listing it as \"foo\") would result in a managed entry that can never be discovered by exec.LookPath(\"entire-foo\"). Consider only stripping extensions on Windows (or alternatively, enforce/normalize the installed filename to exactly `entire-<name>` on Unix) so managed installs actually resolve at runtime.\n\n================================================================================\n[Copilot] cmd/entire/cli/plugin_store.go:227\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInstallPluginFromPath derives the bare plugin name from the source basename but doesn't validate it against the runtime dispatch rules (e.g., `agent-*` is explicitly reserved/never dispatched, and names like \".\"/\"..\" should be rejected to keep data-dir isolation). As a result, `entire plugin install /path/to/entire-agent-foo` can succeed even though `entire agent-foo` will never dispatch. Consider validating the derived bare name with the same rules as isPluginCandidate (or a shared validator) and returning a clear error when the plugin name is not dispatchable.\n\n================================================================================\n[Copilot] cmd/entire/cli/plugin_group.go:25\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe help text hard-codes `~/.local/share/entire/plugins/bin` as the managed directory, but the actual resolution prefers $XDG_DATA_HOME/entire/plugins/bin on Unix and %LOCALAPPDATA%\\entire\\plugins\\bin on Windows (plus $ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DIR/bin override). Consider updating the Long description to match the real precedence so users on XDG setups / Windows aren't misled.\n\n\n================================================================================\n[Copilot] cmd/entire/cli/root.go:88\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRegistering the built-in `entire plugin` command means an existing external command named `entire-plugin` (previously invocable as `entire plugin` via the dispatcher) will now be shadowed permanently because built-ins always win. If this is intended, consider calling it out in the external-commands docs / release notes, or choosing a less collision-prone built-in name (e.g., `plugins`) to reduce the chance of breaking an existing workflow.\n\n\n================================================================================\n[cursor[bot]] cmd/entire/cli/plugin_store.go:224\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Install accepts unrunnable names\n\n**Medium Severity**\n\n<!-- DESCRIPTION START -->\n`InstallPluginFromPath` only checks the `entire-` prefix, so it can install names like `entire-agent-*` or `entire--foo` that `resolvePlugin` always rejects. `entire plugin install` can report success for entries that can never be invoked.\n<!-- DESCRIPTION END -->\n\n<!-- BUGBOT_BUG_ID: 14b0d0d2-9595-4fe2-bddd-7e7c73aa67ae -->\n\n<!-- LOCATIONS START\ncmd/entire/cli/plugin_store.go#L220-L224\ncmd/entire/cli/plugin.go#L118-L130\nLOCATIONS END -->\n<details>\n<summary>Additional Locations (1)</summary>\n\n- [`cmd/entire/cli/plugin.go#L118-L130`](https://github.com/entireio/cli/blob/700abdb19b82ab7249546eeb5fe9a222ca742501/cmd/entire/cli/plugin.go#L118-L130)\n\n</details>\n\n<div><a href=\"https://cursor.com/open?REDACTED\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-light.png\"><img alt=\"Fix in Cursor\" width=\"115\" height=\"28\" src=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;<a href=\"https://cursor.com/agents?REDACTED\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-light.png\"><img alt=\"Fix in Web\" width=\"99\" height=\"28\" src=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\"></picture></a></div>\n\n\n<sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 700abdb19b82ab7249546eeb5fe9a222ca742501. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n\n\n================================================================================\n[cursor[bot]] cmd/entire/cli/plugin_store.go:247\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Force install can delete source\n\n**Medium Severity**\n\n<!-- DESCRIPTION START -->\nWhen `SourcePath` already equals the managed destination, `--force` removes `dest`, which is also the source file, then creates a self-referential symlink. This can delete a manually dropped managed plugin and leave it broken.\n<!-- DESCRIPTION END -->\n\n<!-- BUGBOT_BUG_ID: 39ef07c0-d94c-4e7a-b6d8-a66e06fea6b8 -->\n\n<!-- LOCATIONS START\ncmd/entire/cli/plugin_store.go#L234-L247\nLOCATIONS END -->\n<div><a href=\"https://cursor.com/open?REDACTED\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-light.png\"><img alt=\"Fix in Cursor\" width=\"115\" height=\"28\" src=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-cursor-dark.png\"></picture></a>&nbsp;<a href=\"https://cursor.com/agents?REDACTED\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-light.png\"><img alt=\"Fix in Web\" width=\"99\" height=\"28\" src=\"https://cursor.com/assets/images/fix-in-web-dark.png\"></picture></a></div>\n\n\n<sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 700abdb19b82ab7249546eeb5fe9a222ca742501. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n\n\n================================================================================\n[cursor[bot]] cmd/entire/cli/plugin_store.go:79\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n### Data dir can escape\n\n**Medium Severity**\n\n<!-- DESCRIPTI